 primitive roots modulo primes. It remains open in general, although important conditional and partial results are known.\nL23: \nL24: References\nL25: ## Primary source\nL26: \nL27: Gabriele Fici, Estéban Gabory, Giuseppe Romana and Marinella Sciortino, “Unclustered BWTs of any Length over Non-Binary Alphabets”, cite15†arXiv:2508.20879†arxiv.org (2025).\nL28: ## Additional references\nL29: 15 papers in this index state this conjecture (2012–2025).\nL30: The statement above is taken from the most recent of them; the others are cite16†arXiv:2507.13548†arxiv.org , cite17†arXiv:2502.12844†arxiv.org , cite18†arXiv:2410.09694†arxiv.org , cite19†arXiv:2402.03280†arxiv.org , cite20†arXiv:2312.11258†arxiv.org , cite21†arXiv:2107.12121†arxiv.org , cite22†arXiv:2107.12123†arxiv.org , cite23†arXiv:2006.15683†arxiv.org , cite24†arXiv:1906.07446†arxiv.org , cite25†arXiv:1809.09811†arxiv.org , cite26†arXiv:1408.0602†arxiv.org , cite27†arXiv:1404.4007†arxiv.org , and 2 more.\nL31: cite28†number-theory cite29†primitive-roots L32: \nL33: 0 0\nL34: \nL35: Posted 1 month ago\nL36: ## Progress summary\nL37: \nL38: Refresh Refreshed 1 month ago\nL39: \nL40: Claimed progress\nL41: \nL42: The conjecture remains open, although an undated preprint claims a complete proof that has not been independently verified.\nL43: \nL44: Artin conjectured in 1927 that every admissible integer is a primitive root modulo infinitely many primes.\nL45: \nL46: Known results\nL47:   * Hooley, 1967: proved the conjecture conditionally under the relevant Generalized Riemann Hypothesis.\nL48:   * Gupta–Murty, 1984: proved it for infinitely many integers, without an explicit infinite list.\nL49:   * Heath-Brown, 1986: showed that at most two prime values and at most three squarefree values can be exceptions; in particular, one of $2$2, $3$3, or $5$5 works.\nL50:   * No particular admissible integer is known unconditionally to work.\nL51: \nL52: 2026 claimed proof and new bounds\nL53: An undated version-$14$14 preprint claims an unconditional positive-density asymptotic for every admissible integer, which would settle the conjecture, but supplies no independent verification or referee assessment. On August 25, 2026, a new paper by M. Ram Murty and Sunil Naik was announced on a non-abelian large sieve and Artin’s conjecture; the retrieved record gives no theorem details.\nL54: A 2026 journal article by Chi Wa Chan reports uniform density bounds in quadratic number fields, but its precise advance cannot be assessed from the available record.\nL55: Current status (as of August 2026): Artin’s conjecture remains open unconditionally; Hooley’s conditional theorem and the classical partial results stand, while the claimed complete proof is unverified.\nL56: \nL57: Sources\nL58:   * cite30†scholar.rose-hulman.edu ↗†scholar.rose-hulman.edu L59:   * cite31†mathoverflow.net ↗†mathoverflow.net L60:   * cite32†arxiv.org ↗†arxiv.org L61:   * cite33†doi.org ↗†doi.org L62:   * cite34†hrj.episciences.org ↗†hrj.episciences.org L63:   * cite35†math.dartmouth.edu ↗†math.dartmouth.edu L64:   * cite36†www2.math.upenn.edu ↗†www2.math.upenn.edu L65:   * cite37†pphmjopenaccess.com ↗†pphmjopenaccess.com L66:   * cite38†ejpam.com ↗†www.ejpam.com L67:   * cite39†arxiv.org ↗†arxiv.org L68:   * cite40†arxiv.org ↗†arxiv.org L69:   * cite41†arxiv.org ↗†arxiv.org L70:   * cite42†arxiv.org ↗†www.arxiv.org L71:   * cite43†arxiv.org ↗†arxiv.org L72:   * cite44†mathstodon.xyz ↗†mathstodon.xyz L73:   * cite45†mathstodon.xyz ↗†mathstodon.xyz L74:   * cite46†mathstodon.xyz ↗†mathstodon.xyz L75:   * cite47†scientificamerican.com ↗†www.scientificamerican.com L76:   * cite48†quantamagazine.org ↗†www.quantamagazine.org L77:   * cite49†scientificamerican.com ↗†www.scientificamerican.com L78:   * cite50†quantamagazine.org ↗†www.quantamagazine.org L79:   * cite51†scientificamerican.com ↗†www.scientificamerican.co